---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { t, type Lang } from '../../lib/i18n';

export function getStaticPaths() {
  return [{ params: { lang: 'zh' } }, { params: { lang: 'en' } }];
}

const lang = Astro.params.lang as Lang;
const otherLang: Lang = lang === 'zh' ? 'en' : 'zh';
---

<Base
  title={t(lang, 'about.title')}
  description={
    lang === 'zh'
      ? '关于胡梦雅（Mengya (Mia) Hu）——Responsible AI 方向的应用科学家'
      : 'About Mengya (Mia) Hu — applied scientist working on Responsible AI'
  }
  lang={lang}
  path={`/${lang}/about/`}
  altPath={`/${otherLang}/about/`}
>
  <article class="article">
    <header>
      <h1>{t(lang, 'about.title')}</h1>
    </header>
    <div class="article-body">
      {lang === 'zh' ? (
        <div>
          <p>
            我是胡梦雅（Mengya (Mia) Hu），Microsoft 高级应用科学家，在
            Responsible AI 团队工作，方向是大模型的内容安全：LLM
            内容审核系统、幻觉检测与缓解、安全与体验的权衡设计。
          </p>
          <p>
            在此之前，我在 Princeton
            读博士，做的是系外行星探测——为「星影」（Starshade）望远镜系统建仿真管线，并设计从光子计数图像中识别微弱信号的检测方法。本科毕业于中国科学技术大学。
          </p>
          <p>
            从找行星到管住 AI，听起来跨度很大，但对我来说是同一件事：<strong>在巨大的噪声里，可靠地检测你关心的信号</strong>——那时是恒星光晕旁的一颗暗行星，现在是海量生成内容里的一句有害输出或一处幻觉。
          </p>
          <p>
            这个博客从工程和机制视角写 AI
            安全：可复现的评测、具体的攻防手法、政策落地的实际影响。每篇文章中英双语。
          </p>
          <p>本站所有观点仅代表个人，与雇主无关。</p>
        </div>
      ) : (
        <div>
          <p>
            I'm Mengya (Mia) Hu, a Senior Applied Scientist at Microsoft working
            on Responsible AI. My focus is LLM safety in production: content
            moderation systems, hallucination detection and mitigation, and the
            design trade-offs between safety and user experience.
          </p>
          <p>
            Before that, I did my Ph.D. at Princeton on exoplanet detection —
            building simulation pipelines for a starshade–telescope system and
            designing detection methods that pull faint signals out of
            photon-counting images. I did my undergrad at USTC.
          </p>
          <p>
            Hunting planets and moderating AI sound worlds apart, but to me
            they're the same problem: <strong>reliably detecting the signal you
            care about inside overwhelming noise</strong> — once a dim planet
            beside a star's glare, now a harmful output or a hallucinated claim
            inside oceans of generated text.
          </p>
          <p>
            This blog looks at AI safety from an engineering and mechanistic
            point of view: reproducible evaluations, concrete attack-and-defense
            techniques, and the real-world impact of policy. Every post is
            published in both English and Chinese.
          </p>
          <p>All opinions here are my own and do not represent my employer.</p>
        </div>
      )}
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
